.TH XD\-SHUTDOWN 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-shutdown \- the Shut Down and Log Off dialogs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-shutdown
.OP \-\-logoff
.OP \-\-dry\-run
.YS
.SY xd\-shutdown
.B \-\-action
.I action
.OP \-\-dry\-run
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-shutdown
is the Shut Down Windows dialog: Log off, Shut down, Restart, Stand by and
Hibernate (the last two only if the kernel supports them).
.PP
Shut down, restart, stand by and hibernate run
.BR "systemctl poweroff" ,
.BR reboot ,
.B suspend
and
.BR hibernate ;
logind decides through polkit whether the user may.
Log off ends the session: it ends the XeonDesktop compositor, or, when the
taskbar runs under another compositor, asks logind to end the session.
.PP
Power actions are only carried out in a XeonDesktop session on a seat
.RB ( XEONDESKTOP_NESTED=0 );
in a nested or test session, or outside a XeonDesktop session, they are
only printed, so a test can't power off the computer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-logoff
The Log Off confirmation instead: in the Luna style, XP's Log Off box with
Switch User and Log Off; otherwise Windows 2000's \(lqAre you sure you want
to log off?\(rq.
.TP
.BI \-\-action " action"
Act at once, without a dialog:
.BR logoff ", " shutdown ", " restart ", " standby ", " hibernate ,
or
.B switchuser
(lock the screen and go to the display manager's greeter).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Only print the power actions.
.TP
.BI \-\-style " style"
.TQ
.BI \-\-scheme " file"
The visual style and colour scheme instead of those in
.IR desktop.ini .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XEONDESKTOP_PID
The compositor that Log off ends, set by
.BR xd\-compositor (1).
.TP
.B XEONDESKTOP_NESTED
.B 0
in a session on a seat, where power actions are carried out.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-compositor (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR loginctl (1)
